@h1v9 Essentially, performance improvements are enhancements, not bug fixes. Furthermore, since changes like these may introduce new bugs as a side effect, they should not be merged after the feature freeze. As mentioned earlier, this requires careful consideration. Even if I were to approve it, the product team would likely not.

> For example if an animated node is removed from the scene tree, like with node->get_parent()->remove_child(node), it will still be animated even though it is no longer part of the scene.

> However, if that same tree is packed into a PackedScene and instantiated again, AnimationMixer will fail to resolve the NodePath and report an error, which is inconsistent.

@Ryan-000 So, I assume that addresses issues https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14720 and https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14457. Would it be possible to make a list of cases where errors occur, or would you be able to help with these improvements?

@TokageItLab Done. `clear_cache_on_stop` is now implemented and documented, defaults to true.

Since this is now configurable, fully backward-compatible, and requires no user action unless desired can we get this merged in 4.7?

EDIT: macOS build has failed but it seems a glitch with github actions.  I can force push another commit to restart the checks if needed.
